  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `{cite}` of `requirements.authoring.persistence` on `src/authoring/mod.rs#struct[PendingAssessment]` is the right role.\n\n- **Not a test.** The struct is a data type, not a test or test helper.\n- **Not an `{impl}` root.** The code that persists the assessment is already marked `{impl}` for this requirement: `src/authoring/mod.rs#impl[PendingAssessment]` and `src/authoring/batch.rs#fn[stage_record]`. The struct is the type those items use, so it is reached through them and needs no `{impl}`.\n- **Supported `{cite}`.** The struct holds the `subject` and the JSON `record` that are written out, along with the outcome. The requirement specifies what is persisted: the subject text, determination, rationale and inputs, with all three outcomes counted as completed. A change to that text could require changing the struct's fields, so the `{cite}` is justified.\n- **Not redundant.** The struct has no `{impl}` or `{test}` reference to the same requirement.\n\nI found no gap.",
